# The time zone: `date` in local time, and the clock at the top right of
# the desktop (its box always ends 50 pixels from the right edge).
@disk
$ timezone
time zone: UTC ('timezone UTC|CET|+HH:MM' to change)
$ date
~ ^\d{4}-\d\d-\d\dT\d\d:\d\d:\d\dZ$
@screenshot 1920x1080 pixels 1865,8=1f3a5f 1875,8=a8d0f0
$ timezone cet
time zone: CET (saved)
$ date
~ ^\d{4}-\d\d-\d\d \d\d:\d\d:\d\d CES?T   \(\d{4}-\d\d-\d\dT\d\d:\d\d:\d\dZ\)$
$ cat /system/timezone
CET
$ timezone +05:30
time zone: UTC+05:30 (saved)
$ timezone mars
usage: timezone UTC | CET (Central Europe, with summer time) | +HH:MM | -HH:MM
@reboot
$ timezone
time zone: UTC+05:30 ('timezone UTC|CET|+HH:MM' to change)
$ threads
~ clock +(waiting|ready)
@screenshot 1920x1080 pixels 1865,8=1f3a5f
$ timezone utc
time zone: UTC (saved)
